## Question

Mitochondria are the organelles primarily responsible for producing ATP in a eukaryotic cell.

## Answer Choices

- A. True
- B. False

## Answer

> [!answer]- Reveal answer
> **Correct Answer: True**
>
> Oxidative phosphorylation happens on the inner mitochondrial membrane, which is why mitochondria are called the cell's powerhouse.
